+++++ Learning +++++ :

SQL is a Structure Query language (SQL) 
- Imperative Programming: 
      Imperative programming like python, java, php etc. you write step-by-step instructions to that tells the computer how to work on something. 

- Declarative Programming: 
      First you need to understand what data is sorted in your table, then we need to write query descibing what data you want and pull it from data base management system. 
The database management system understand how to get it. This is called declarative programming

- Before going into learning SQL first we need to undersand the design of databases and how it stores
  - Entity Relationship (ER) diagrams
  - Schemas
  - Table structure and relationships

+++++ Entity Relationship (ER) diagrams:
        An ER diagram is a planning tool used to visualize the structure of a database, It helps you figure out what kind of data you need and how to store them into database, and how all of those pieces of data relate/talk to each other

- Entity : 
      Entity are the main objects or concepts in system, like Person, Dog, Course etc, Entities have attributes that describe them. A person might have name, data of birth and addess etc are attributes.

- Relationships: 
      It describes how the data are connected to each other. Eg A person might adobt a Dog, or a student might enrolle for course.
<img src="data:image/png;base64," />


+++++ Schemas:
      A schemas is another way of describe the structure of a database. It shows the same information as ER, but in more technical and precise the format and focus on how the data will be stored.
Each elements of a shema will become table in a database

Some of the sample schema models which are designed to solve the diff applications requirements
    - Flat Model:
        A flat model schema is a 2-D array which contains rows and columns

    - Hierarchical Model:
        Data is arranged using parent-child relationships and a tree-like structure

    - Network Model:
        It is similar to hierarchical model in that is represents data using nodes(enties) and edge (relationships), it is flexible model to allow many-to-many relationships.

    - Relational Model:
        It is better for desingin obect-oriented programmings

    - Star Schema:
        It is helping for storing and analyzing large amount of data. it contants tow enties "Fact" table contains numerial data and "Dimension" table contains related to dimentions ex. product, time, people etc

    - Snowflake Schema:
        It is just like star schema but the main differance in both models is that in snowflake schema - dimentaions tables are further normalized into multiple related tables. The snowflake schema is used for anlyzing large amount of data.


